:1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"grade\":\"partial\",\"rationale\":\"The answer gets the retention rules right. It says copies of all written AP agreements must be preserved, which matches the accepted supplement for Rule 6c-11(d)(1). It applies the correct period of at least five years, with the first two easily accessible, to both AP agreements and basket records. The central omission is the content of the basket records. The answer only says 'composition of each creation and redemption basket … including the related transaction information.' It leaves out the required elements: holdings identifiers or descriptions, quantities and weights, the custom-basket designation and compliance statement where applicable, the cash balancing amount, and the identity of the transacting AP. Those specifics are a core part of what the question asks, so this is a substantive omission rather than a material error. The live-source caveat does not affect the grade.\"}","ttft_ms":2180,"type":"result","duration_ms":4296,"uuid":"85e6b3cd-74b9-4bc9-b207-0d5b7c5ff779","ttft_stream_ms":543,"time_to_request_ms":68,"first_content_frame_ms":543,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
